{% doc %}
  @prompt
    Create a 4-column horizontal timeline/process block on a soft pale mint-green background. Each column represents a stage and includes, top to bottom:
    
    A small filled dark green circle (bullet dot) followed by a thin horizontal line extending to the right, aligned at the top of the column
    A small uppercase label in dark green, letter-spaced (e.g., 'DAYS 1–5', 'DAYS 6–15', 'DAYS 16–20', 'LAUNCH DAY')
    A large serif heading below it in dark green/black (e.g., Sketch, Build, Test, Ship)
    A short 2-line description in muted grey sans-serif text explaining that stage
    
    Repeat this structure for 4 columns total, evenly spaced with equal gutters between them. Keep generous padding around the whole section. Typography should mix a serif font for headings (elegant, editorial) with a clean sans-serif for labels and body text — matching a premium, minimal design studio aesthetic. No borders or boxes around each column — just the dot-and-line divider at the top of each to visually separate them, Also add the above line to Launch day
{% enddoc %}
